{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Gone: /cart stops being a page at all.

  The store has two carts and only one of them is maintained. Every override in
  this theme -- the upsell rows, the totals breakdown, the variant pickers, the
  SAVED % badges -- is built against the drawer. The /cart page misses most of
  them, so it is not just a second cart, it is a worse one.

  pg-no-cart-page already intercepts links to /cart and bounces direct visits,
  and it still does the link half. But it renders from footer-group, which means
  it runs only AFTER the entire cart page has been built and painted: the
  shopper sees the old cart, then it disappears. Its 4-second failsafe actively
  reveals the page rather than hiding it, which is the right call for a script
  that might fail -- but it means the page is never truly gone.

  So the page is removed at the template instead. templates/cart.json renders
  this section and nothing else: no pg-cart-header, no pg-cart-main. There is no
  cart page left to flash, because none is built. The redirect below is the
  first thing in the body and runs during parse, before anything downstream.

  WHY STILL JAVASCRIPT. Shopify's URL redirects only fire on a 404, and /cart is
  a live core route that never 404s, so it cannot be redirected server-side.
  Liquid has no redirect either. A parse-time script is as early as this can
  happen.

  The sessionStorage flag is the one pg-no-cart-page already reads on arrival to
  open the drawer, so the two stay in step -- set here, consumed there, cleared
  on read.

  noindex matters more than it looks: /cart is a real crawlable URL, and a cart
  page in the index is a bad search result that lands shoppers on a redirect.

  NOTE ON templates/cart.json. Shopify's theme editor regenerates that file from
  its own state on save, so if the cart template is ever opened and saved in the
  customiser it may pull the old sections back. If a full cart page reappears,
  that is the first thing to check.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function(){
  /* exactly the cart page, with or without a locale prefix -- never the
     /cart/add, /cart/change, /cart/update endpoints the cart posts to */
  if (!/^\/(?:[a-z]{2}(?:-[a-z]{2})?\/)?cart\/?$/i.test(location.pathname)) return;

  try { sessionStorage.setItem('pgOpenDrawer', '1'); } catch (e){}

  var back = '/';
  try {
    var ref = document.referrer ? new URL(document.referrer) : null;
    if (ref && ref.origin === location.origin &&
        !/^\/(?:[a-z]{2}(?:-[a-z]{2})?\/)?cart\/?$/i.test(ref.pathname)){
      back = ref.pathname + ref.search;
    }
  } catch (e){}

  /* replace, not assign: the cart page must not sit in the back stack, or Back
     from the homepage returns to it and bounces again */
  location.replace(back);
})();
</script>
<noscript>
  <style>.pg-cart-gone{max-width:520px;margin:80px auto;padding:0 20px;text-align:center;color:#F1EDF7;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}</style>
  <div class="pg-cart-gone">
    <h1>Your cart</h1>
    <p>Your cart opens from the bag icon at the top of every page.</p>
    <p><a href="/">Continue shopping</a></p>
  </div>
</noscript>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Gone", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
